Subject: [PATCH] GPU renderer: the glare shuffle done on the buffer itself

Transformers' glare (Antarctica, also in Amazon) makes its frame's alpha
byte from the scene's green: sprites through a 16-bit view of the 32-bit
frame onto the same view, 8 columns over (a block row's columns 8-15 are
the high halves of the words whose low halves are 0-7), FBMSK 0x3FFF
(RGBA8888's: the 16-bit pixels' bits 8-15 written). Drawn as it is, the
16-bit view took the whole scene through local memory and back, a GS
pixel a value: Antarctica at the PS2's resolution at any scale. Now the
draws are left out and each word's alpha byte made its green byte on the
buffer, a GL pixel at a time (PS2X_GPU_COLOUR_SHUFFLE=0: as before).
Scale 1, Amazon: the same picture to the pixel.

Also PS2X_GPU_DRAWLOG_VERTS=1: the vertices of draws to 16-bit frames in
the draw log.
